From 08d32d9c586c18c059a0024db5383160993b5660 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:55:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 155/156] media: i2c: imx586: Add a 2000x1500 4x4 binned mode

Like the main camera: a 4x4 binned 2000x1500 mode over the full field of
view, with the binning and readout registers of the stock 2000x1128 mode
and the PLL settings of the 4000x3000 mode, so the link frequency stays at
421.2 MHz. The default frame length gives 60 fps.
---
 drivers/media/i2c/imx586.c | 126 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 126 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx586.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx586.c
index 1fcb7a023..3ace68384 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx586.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx586.c
@@ -1925,6 +1925,113 @@ static const struct cci_reg_sequence imx586_4000x3000_regs[] = {
 	{ CCI_REG8(0xa678), 0x20 },
 };
 
